r/cleanup-tmp.service\\n     [Unit]\\n     Description=Cleanup /tmp\\n\\n     [Service]\\n     Type=oneshot\\n     Environment=RETENTION_HOURS=24\\n     ExecStart=/workspace/cleanup-tmp.sh\\n  2) ~/.config/systemd/user/cleanup-tmp.timer\\n     [Unit]\\n     Description=Run cleanup /tmp hourly\\n\\n     [Timer]\\n     OnCalendar=hourly\\n     Persistent=true\\n\\n     [Install]\\n     WantedBy=timers.target\\n  - Activate: systemctl --user daemon-reload &amp;&amp; systemctl --user enable --now cleanup-tmp.timer\\n\\nManual run and testing\\n- Run once now: RETENTION_HOURS=24 /workspace/cleanup-tmp.sh\\n- Safe test in a sandbox dir:\\n  - mkdir -p /tmp/testtmp &amp;&amp; : &gt;/tmp/testtmp/old.log\\n  - sleep 65  # ensure it\u2019s older than 1 minute\\n  - TMPDIR=/tmp/testtmp RETENTION_HOURS=0 /workspace/cleanup-tmp.sh\\n\\nNotes\\n- You can tune retention by exporting RETENTION_HOURS (e.g., 12 for 12h).\\n- If crontab/systemd aren\u2019t available on your host, use the manual run or integrate with your scheduler.\\n\\nIf you want, I can attempt to install and verify the cron entry on this machine, but some sandbox environments don\u2019t include cron/systemd services by default.', task_completed='true', outputs={}, thought='', action='finish')], inputs={}, outputs={}, agent_state=<AgentState.FINISHED: 'finished'>, resume_state=None, traffic_control_state=<TrafficControlState.NORMAL: 'normal'>, metrics=Metrics({'accumulated_cost': 0.17361525000000003, 'costs': [{'model': 'gpt-5', 'cost': 0.0026755, 'timestamp': 1779376613.0788107}, {'model': 'gpt-5', 'cost': 0.061776750000000005, 'timestamp': 1779376679.1196103}, {'model': 'gpt-5', 'cost': 0.031927500000000004, 'timestamp': 1779376713.216613}, {'model': 'gpt-5', 'cost': 0.0193825, 'timestamp': 1779376733.9968202}, {'model': 'gpt-5', 'cost': 0.0186985, 'timestamp': 1779376749.7130642}, {'model': 'gpt-5', 'cost': 0.006692750000000001, 'timestamp': 1779376795.5999238}, {'model': 'gpt-5', 'cost': 0.013608, 'timestamp': 1